<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov aluminium imports rise 14.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov aluminium imports rise 14.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium imports rose to 233,013 tonnes in November, up 14.9 percent from 202,878 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry statistics released on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		  Nov 96	    Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Total	  233,013	   255,219     202,878</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Brazil	  50,374	    25,617	30,772</p>
<p> Russia	  28,648	    56,103	31,220</p>
<p> Australia     30,230	    35,340	38,638</p>
<p> U.S.	    14,950	    22,585	19,341</p>
<p>Refined aluminium imports in the first 11 months of 1996 were 2,550,414 tonnes, off 1.1 percent from 2,579,032 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
